  "priorExpiration": "2004-07-23",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 3003.02 Hardship Registration Notice.\n\n(a) Upon receipt of an abstract of conviction of an offense set forth in Saf-C 3003.01(b) - (e) or a habitual offender certification order, the supervisor of financial responsibility shall issue a notice to the person whose license is under suspension or revocation.\n\n(b) The notice shall include the following information:\n\n(1) A statement that all registrations issued in the person's name shall be suspended in 30 days;\n\n(2) A statement that all registrations and plates shall be forwarded to the department at the\n\nconclusion of the 30-day period, unless a hardship registration has been obtained within the 30-day period;\n\n(3) The procedure for obtaining a hardship registration; and\n\n(4) A statement that the person shall be required to present the registration suspension notice to the department, if a hardship registration shall be requested, in order to prove that the person is qualified, pursuant to RSA 261:180 III, to obtain a hardship registration.\n\nSource. #5027, eff 12-19-90; ss by #6296, eff 7-23-96, EXPIRED: 7-23-04\n\nNew. #8181, eff 9-25-04; ss by #10085, eff 1-31-12; ss by #13279, eff 10-19-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c3000.html"
